cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use bitg in research or a publication, please cite it as below."
title: "bitg: input method and converter for the 2026 Uzbek Latin alphabet"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "dtwinuz and bitg contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/dtwinuz/bitg/graphs/contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dtwinuz/bitg"
url: "https://bitg.uz"
abstract: >-
  bitg converts Uzbek text to the 2026 Latin alphabet (ö, ğ, ş, ç, ʼ) while you type. It ships input methods for
  Windows (TSF), Linux (IBus, Fcitx5) and macOS (InputMethodKit), a command-line converter for text and documents,
  and restores missing apostrophes from a frequency lexicon while keeping English words and brand names unchanged.
keywords:
  - Uzbek
  - Latin alphabet
  - input method
  - transliteration
  - keyboard
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
version: "0.3.1"
date-released: "2026-11-12"
